  "question": {
    "text": "An online exam is attempted by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>&nbsp;candidates out of which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn></math> are boys. The average marks obtained by boys is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math> with a variance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The variance of marks obtained by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math> girls is also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The average marks of all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> candidates is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math> is the average marks of girls and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is the variance of marks of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> candidates, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
